          "say": "GPU memory combines neighboring lane accesses into regions. For this scalar float model, a full aligned warp reads adjacent words across four thirty-two-byte sectors. The naive transpose reads that way, then writes with a whole matrix row between neighboring lanes. Its output payload becomes scattered.",
